# Lines of the kit that no-form-rules.test.sh lets pass: they describe what the user types, not how
# the kit writes. One entry a line, `<path>:<fixed text of the line>`; a hit passes when its path is
# <path> and its line contains the text.
commands/pr/learn.md:argument-hint: "<PR> [area in plain words
commands/pr/review.md:argument-hint: "<PR number or URL> [instructions in plain words]"
commands/pr/sync.md:argument-hint: "[context in plain words] [--no-push]"
skills/plan/run/SKILL.md:or a list in plain words.
skills/pr/learn/SKILL.md:an area, in plain words: the reading below goes deeper there
README.md:ask in plain words ("explain PR 456", "run the plan")
